        {
          "id": 3379919884,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hi,\nThanks for your reply.\n\nHere is the pcapng file generated using the same request shown in my screenshot. I am not sure how Linux handles this architecture.\n\nOn FreeBSD, the BPF program is attached to the USB bus per HCI device. This means you must filter by the correct device to get meaningful output; otherwise, you may capture traffic from other devices as well.\n\nIn this sample, you can filter using usb.address or usb.device_address == 11.\n\n[usb_sample.pcapng](/uploads/a86b0e40a6e59bfc6f52c14afb38768a/usb_sample.pcapng)",
          "author": {
            "id": 12498601,
            "username": "aokblast",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "aokblast",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/12498601/avatar.png?v=1788226909",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/aokblast"
