      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3379996341,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Since `dissect_freebsd_usb_frames` seems to be called in all the cases above, and `dissect_usb_payload` is never called with these FreeBSD frames (because `dissect_freebsd_usb_frames` advances the offset to the end), would it be clearer to just have\n\n```c\nif (header_type == USB_HEADER_FREEBSD) {\n    dissect_freebsd_usb_frames(tree, tvb, offset);\n} else {\n    dissect_usb_payload(tvb, pinfo, parent, tree, urb, urb_type, offset, device_address);\n}\n```\n\nhere instead of calling `dissect_freebsd_usb_frames` in so many places above?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
